Use a fixed ld-seed in PositionRestraintCommTest.PositionRestraintsTwoCOMs.

The test uses tcoupl = v-rescale, whose stochastic term is driven by ld-seed,
but its mdp string does not set ld-seed, so grompp picks a random seed on every
run. The step-10 "Position Rest." energy then varies from run to run
(sd 0.30 on a reference of 64.72, i.e. 0.47% relative) and falls outside the
1.5e-2 relative tolerance used for double precision in ~0.5% of runs, making
MdrunTestsOneRank/MdrunTestsTwoRanks fail at random.
Set the same fixed seed (234262) that the test simulation database uses for
its generated mdp files, as other mdrun tests with v-rescale already do
(see src/programs/mdrun/tests/multisimtest.cpp).
Test added in https://gitlab.com/gromacs/gromacs/-/commit/b68acdf40ad5be55d9fba58802b9700547011946
